+/**
+ * @brief Precise geometry for a matrix the port knows more exactly
+ *
+ * The game builds its model matrices with whole-number steps, so body parts
+ * shake by a fraction of a unit as a model moves. A port that keeps the same
+ * matrix at full precision passes it here right after loading the integer
+ * one into the GTE: r is the rotation in the GTE's units (4096 = 1.0), row
+ * by row, t the translation. Projections use it for their exact positions
+ * while the GTE still holds that integer matrix.
+ */
+void Psyz_PgxpSetFloatMatrix(const float r[9], const float t[3]);
+void Psyz_PgxpClearFloatMatrix(void);
+
